.TH vmstatlog 8 "15 Aug 2026" "" "ClusterTools2"
.\"
.SH NAME
vmstatlog \- log the vmstat with timestamp
.\"
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vmstatlog \fI[ logfile ]\fR
.\"
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBvmstatlog\fP logs the vmtstat with timestamp.
Basically the script puts the output of "date +%F %T" in front of each line for the output of "cat /proc/vmstat".
.br
.\"
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
To run vmstatlog every 10 minutes, the crontab entry could look like this:
.br
-01-56/10 * * * * root /usr/sbin/vmstatlog /var/log/vmstat.log
.TP
To rotate and compress the log from time to time, the logrotate entry could look like this:
.br
/var/log/vmstat.log {
    compress
    dateext
    maxage 365
    rotate 99
    size +2M
    notifempty
    missingok
    copytruncate
.br
}
.\"
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
Successful program execution.
.br
.B >0 
Usage, syntax or execution errors.
.\"
.SH FILES
.TP
/usr/sbin/vmstatlog
the script itself.
.TP
/var/log/vmstat.log
the default logfile.
.TP
/etc/cron.d/ClusterTools2
the cron entry.
.TP
/etc/logrotate.d/ClusterTools2
the logrotate entry.
.\"
.SH BUGS
Feedback is welcome, please mail to feedback@suse.com
.\"
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBproc\fP(5), \fBvmstat\fP(8), \fBcrontab\fP(5), \fBlogrotate\fP(8), \fBClusterTools2\fP(7)
